 "final_result": "Built a three-script Python workflow for cubic perovskite CsPbBr3 (Pm-3m, #221) from scratch.\n\nMaterials Project ID: mp-600089 (0.025 eV/atom above hull, band_gap_eV ~1.78, non-magnetic).\n\nAtom count: 5 atoms before and after primitive-cell reduction (the MP structure was already primitive; space group Pm-3m #221 unchanged).\n\nWorkflow outline:\n1. generate_cif fetched the base CsPbBr3 structure (mp-600089, Pm-3m #221) into structures/base_CsPbBr3.cif. reduce_cell.py reduced it to the primitive cell via chem_llm.kpath (kp_atoms(standard_kpath(atoms))) and wrote structures/structure_000.cif.\n2. generate_structures.py (ran OK, returncode 0) generated 51 structures (structure_000.cif through structure_050.cif). structure_000 is unperturbed; 001-050 have random thermal displacements (T=300 K, the room-temperature cubic phase; U in A^2: Cs=0.005, Pb=0.003, Br=0.008; per-axis RMS = sqrt(U) in A) plus small random lattice strain (Frobenius norm 1%). INVARIANT 1 (nat/ntyp) asserted per structure.\n3. Pseudopotentials fetched (nc, pbesol, stringent, UPF, scalar-relativistic -- Pb Z=82 > 54 but no spin-orbit physics targeted, so sr is correct per DECISION RULE; hint_level='normal' as a balance between accuracy and cost). z_valence: Cs=9, Pb=22, Br=17. Total electrons = 82, occupied bands = 41. Recommended cutoffs (Ha): Cs=25, Pb=44, Br=38. Max = 44 Ha = 88 Ry (INVARIANT 5 conversion: 1 Ha = 2 Ry). ecutwfc=88 Ry, ecutrho=352 Ry.\n4. setup_jobs.py (ran OK, returncode 0) created calculations/NNN/ for all 51 structures with: pseudopotential files, kpath.json (from chem_llm.kpath), pw.in (SCF, k-mesh 5x5x5 from scf_kmesh(prim, metal=False)), bands.in (NSCF, kpts=kp_kpts(kp), nbnd=64), and bands_post.in (bands.x, lsym=.false.). validate_qe_input passed on calculations/000/pw.in and calculations/000/bands.in (nat=5, ntyp=3, no issues).\n5. run_espresso_workflow returned success: true for calculations/000 (scf 7.0s, bands_scf 86.2s, bands_post 11.4s). pw.out confirms 82 electrons, 41 occupied bands (consistent with nbnd=64).\n6. plot_bands.py (ran OK, returncode 0) used chem_llm.kpath.plot_axis for the x-axis/ticks/segments, chem_llm.qe_output.read_pw_out for n_occupied, and band_edges for VBM/CBM/gap. Aligned to VBM (semiconductor). Saved calculations/000/bands_000.pdf.\n\nASE functions used: ase.io.read (CIF), ase.io.write (CIF), ase.io.espresso.write_espresso_in (pw.x inputs), ase.Atoms (structure representation). No pymatgen imports.\n\nBand gap obtained: 1.60 eV (VBM at 4.5210 eV, CBM at 6.1210 eV in the raw bands.dat; aligned to VBM=0). This is slightly below the MP value of 1.78 eV, which is expected for PBEsol (a known underestimator of band gaps).\n\nScientific assumptions:\n- T=300 K: the cubic Pm-3m phase is the room-temperature phase of CsPbBr3 (tetragonal below ~230 K, orthorhombic below ~160 K).\n- Scalar-relativistic pseudopotentials: Pb is Z=82 > 54, but the task does not target spin-orbit-coupled physics (no topological states, no Rashba splitting), so sr is appropriate per the DECISION RULE.\n- occupations='fixed': CsPbBr3 is a clear semiconductor (gap ~1.78 eV), not a metal.\n- nspin=1: non-magnetic (moment_per_formula_unit_muB = 0.0).\n- ecutwfc=88 Ry (2x the max recommended 44 Ha from Pb), ecutrho=352 Ry (4x ecutwfc).\n- nbnd=64: 41 occupied bands + comfortable margin.\n- SCF k-mesh 5x5x5: from scf_kmesh(prim, metal=False), appropriate for a semiconductor with a ~6 A cubic cell.\n\nItems for expert review:\n- The PBEsol band gap (1.60 eV) is lower than the experimental/MP value (~1.78 eV); hybrid functionals (HSE06) would give a more accurate gap.\n- The Debye-Waller amplitudes (U values) are representative estimates, not from a phonon calculation; a proper phonon calculation would give temperature-dependent U values.\n- The 1% random strain is a rough model of lattice distortion; a proper molecular dynamics run would give more realistic structural fluctuations.",
